# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and set your own values.
#
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API:
#   - Project URL -> VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   - Public client key (any one of the following; RLS still applies):
#       VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY           (JWT anon key)
#       VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY    (sb_publishable_… from install wizard)
#       VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_DEFAULT_KEY  (same; older name in this repo)
#
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional: skip the login screen while Google SSO is still a placeholder (dev / design review)
# VITE_LOGIN_SKIP_AUTH=true

# Workspace password for the login screen (default is Engineering1 if unset)
# VITE_APP_ACCESS_PASSWORD=Engineering1

# Optional website placeholders (only if needed in your app logic later):
# VITE_APP_WEB_URL=https://your-app-domain.com
# VITE_API_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-webhook-endpoint.example.com

# Local Supabase (Docker): use http://127.0.0.1:54321 + key from `npx supabase status` in .env.local instead.
#
# --- Supabase CLI (gitignored files; never commit) ---
# Personal access token (Dashboard → Account → Access tokens), for `npm run supabase:migrate:hosted`:
#   File: `.env.supabase-cli.local`  →  SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_...
# Postgres URI for same command + `supabase:db:push:remote`:
#   File: `.env.supabase-db.local`   →  SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://...
# If you pasted a token in chat, revoke it and create a new one before using it here.

#   SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:<PASSWORD>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# or use Session pooler URI if IPv4/direct fails — then run:
#   npm run supabase:db:push:remote -- --dry-run
#   npm run supabase:db:push:remote
# Encode special chars in passwords. Alternative: export SUPABASE_DB_URL in the shell.
#
# Copy **public schema data only** old → new (requires `brew install libpq`; run after migrations on NEW):
#   `.env.supabase-copy.local` (gitignored):
#     SOURCE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://... OLD project ...
#     TARGET_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://... NEW project (same URI as SUPABASE_DB_URL OK) ...
#   npm run supabase:copy:data
# OAuth users (`auth.users`) stay on NEW only—everyone re-signs in.

# ── Deloitte / DTTL email SSO (Microsoft Entra ID) via Supabase Auth ───────────────────────────────
#
# Secrets (client secret VALUE) NEVER go in Vite—they belong only in:
#   - Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Azure (hosted / cloud), OR
#   - `supabase/config.toml` + env for local Docker (see [auth.external.azure] block).
#
# 1) Azure Portal → Microsoft Entra ID → App registrations → your app:
#    - Authentication → Add a platform → Web (confidential / server-side OAuth via Supabase):
#          Redirect URI (exact):
#          https://<YOUR_PROJECT_REF>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#      Do not use “SPA” alone for this flow—Supabase exchanges the code with your client secret.
#      (Hosted Supabase completes OAuth here, then redirects the user back to this app.)
#    - Certificates & secrets → New client secret → copy the secret VALUE immediately.
#      Your app listing showed 0 secrets—you must create one before Supabase can complete sign-in.
#    - API permissions: default Microsoft Graph (openid/profile/email/sign-in/read user)
#      must show as granted; admins may need to “Grant admin consent” for tenant-wide SSO.
#
#    Optional hardening / claims (recommended by Supabase docs): Manifest → optionalClaims → add email
#    and optional xms_edov tokens so Entra-ID email verification stance is clearer.
#
# 2) Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Azure → Enable:
#    - Client ID               = Azure “Application (client) ID”
#    - Client Secret Value     = the new secret from step 1
#    - Azure Tenant URL       = REQUIRED for Single tenant (“My organization only”) apps:
#          https://login.microsoftonline.com/<YOUR_DIRECTORY_TENANT_ID>
#      (Matches “Accounts in this organizational directory only”; without this, `/common`
#       flows can mismatch a single-tenant registration.)
#
# 3) Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration:
#    - Site URL               = canonical production Alloc8 URL
#    - Redirect URLs          = wildcard allowlist patterns for everywhere users land after SSO,
#      e.g. http://localhost:5173/** and your deployed origin(s).
#
# 4) This repo (already implemented): Continue with Deloitte email → supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'azure', ... })
#
# 5) Programmatic provisioning (CLI + hosted Management API — run on your laptop with Entra Azure CLI access):
#
#       npm run sso:configure
#       npm run sso:configure -- --dry-run
#       npm run sso:configure -- --azure-only --create-azure-secret
#       npm run sso:configure -- --supabase-only
#
#    Put PAT + identities in `.env.sso.local` (gitignored), for example:
#       SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_personal_access_token
#       VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co      # derives SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF
#       AZURE_APPLICATION_CLIENT_ID=<application (client) id>
#       AZURE_DIRECTORY_TENANT_ID=<directory (tenant) id>
#       AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=<optional; omit if using --create-azure-secret on full run>
#       SITE_URL=https://your-nonprod-alloc8.example/            # merges into uri_allow_list as SITE_URL/**
#       URI_ALLOW_LIST_EXTRA=https://other-host.example/**
#
#    See scripts/configure-deloitte-sso.mjs header for prerequisites (az login, token scopes).

# Optional: steer the Microsoft picker toward your corp domain (`domain_hint`; confirm with IAM which domain applies):
# VITE_SSO_EMAIL_DOMAIN=deloitte.com.au
#
# Local `supabase start` OAuth: set SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_AZURE_SECRET in `supabase/.env` or shell,
# uncomment/fill `[auth.external.azure]` in supabase/config.toml, set `external_url` if testing Azure flows locally.
